			<div class="content" id="post-content-2381399">
									

<p>Had to downvote this SCP due to the odd usage of prehispanic gods and poor research on the subject.</p>
<p>First of all, the Yucatan peninsula was inhabited by mayans, not by mexicas (aztecs) so it doesn't make sense to use mexica's gods in a geographic area occupied by a completely different civilization.</p>
<p>Second, Tlaloc (aztec god) <em>is</em> the water cycle (not <em>the god of</em> xxxxx), and its mayan counterpart is Chaac.</p>
<p>Third, Tlaloc is not the god of fertility, that's the Coatlicue for the Aztecs and Ixchel for the Mayans.</p>

							</div>

								
					
